Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:23:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 0024] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: Nuzlocke (graveyard, fallen kept fallen, Classic locked)

A run made with Nuzlocke on carries nuzlocke.json beside its patch. A new
game of such a run starts a Nuzlocke game (new game id). Each frame of
play: a player unit that falls (force 4) is written at once to
<data>/rando/<title>/nuzlocke/<game id>.json (the Python Ledger format;
Corrin is never written); a graveyard person found in force 0 or 3 with
no map actor (Unit +0xB8 == 0) is moved back to force 4 the way
Unit::TransferImpl(unit, 4, 1) does it; Casual or Phoenix is switched
back to Classic at New Game and in My Castle, with a log line. People
are keyed by their labels' cp932 bytes (label_key, Python pid_key). The
slot side file and the state sidecar name the game id; a state of the
same run keeps its game. Without nuzlocke.json nothing new reads or
writes memory or files (Session.nuz stays None; the side file is
byte-identical to before).

Round 60 track e2 (docs/rando/NUZLOCKE.md section 6), merged on top of
0022 and 0023 in the assemble step.
